{"archetypes":[{"name":"shell-portability","focus_area":"code-quality","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff adds a Bash helper whose behavior depends on Bash 3.2-safe syntax, tolerant probes, and careful option handling.","prompt_body":"Investigate the new shell helper for Bash 3.2 compatibility, quoting, array expansion, unset-variable behavior, and accidental exits around fallible probes. Pay special attention to whether validation paths reliably create logs and return the intended status instead of being short-circuited by shell semantics. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"state-handshake","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The change moves Step 8+ OOS gate plumbing from prompt text into a script while preserving orchestrator-owned state transitions.","prompt_body":"Check that the extracted checkpoint preserves the Step 8+ handoff boundaries between helper and orchestrator. Verify that exit codes, OOS_PENDING clearing, run-statistics emission, and pr-create re-entry remain aligned with the plan and do not create new stuck or unsafe states. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"audit-trail","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The new helper is responsible for durable failure logging, which is central to the accepted reviewer refinements.","prompt_body":"Examine every non-zero path through the checkpoint helper for reliable execution-issues logging with the correct site, output file, tool name, and saved return code. Include pre-gate validation failures, gate rc 1, gate rc 2, append failure behavior, and cases where tmpdir or log paths are missing or unwritable. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"fixture-realism","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The expanded harness uses synthetic git repositories and tmpdirs to assert subtle range and discovery behavior.","prompt_body":"Review the new test cases for whether they genuinely exercise the production behaviors described in the plan. Look for false positives from overly permissive fixtures, missing assertions around stderr and execution-issues contents, git-range setup mistakes, or cleanup/isolation problems that could hide regressions. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
